meta {
  name: Initiate File Upload
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/files
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "mime_type": "image/png",
  //   "artpiece_id": "{{artpieceId}}",
    "name": "sketch.png",
    "notes": "Optional notes about this file.",
    "extension": "png"
  }
}

docs {
  ## Response

  Image mime types return a `thumbnail_upload_url` (presigned PUT to R2) alongside
  the regular `upload_url`. The client must PUT the generated thumbnail blob to that
  URL before calling complete. Non-image types return `thumbnail_upload_url: null`.

  ```json
  {
    "id": "uuid",
    "upload_url": "https://...",
    "thumbnail_upload_url": "https://... | null",
    "expires_at": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"
  }
  ```
}
